{"id":86305,"title":"Medical Volume Rendering Techniques","url":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/1802.07710v1","final_url":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/1802.07710","year":2018,"kind":"web","source":"ddg","doi":"10.48550/arxiv.1802.07710","arxiv":"1802.07710","sha256":"7ef3d7d86b24249bd9b95c55050362193dd2f8dba2367e84a70841206a8dd81d","ctype":"application/pdf","text_src":"arxiv","fetched_at":1793148203.3794582,"text_chars":122138,"abstract":"Medical visualization is the use of computers to create 3D images from medical imaging data sets, almost all surgery and cancer treatment in the developed world relies on it.Volume visualization techniques includes iso-surface visualization, mesh visualization and point cloud visualization techniques, these techniques have revolutionized medicine. Much of modern medicine relies on the 3D imaging that is possible with magnetic resonance imaging (MRI) scanners, functional magnetic resonance imaging (fMRI)scanners, positron emission tomography (PET) scanners, ultrasound imaging (US) scanners, X-Ray scanners, bio-marker microscopy imaging scanners and computed tomography (CT) scanners, which make 3D images out of 2D slices. The primary goal of this report is the application-oriented optimization of existing volume rendering methods providing interactive frame rates. Techniques are presented for traditional alpha-blending rendering, surface-shaded display, maximum intensity projection (MIP), and fast previewing with fully interactive parameter control. Different preprocessing strategies are proposed for interactive iso-surface rendering and fast previewing, such as the well-known marching cube algorithm.","file":null,"marks":["unofficial"],"links":["https://arxiv.org/pdf/1802.07710","https://arxiv.org/pdf/1802.07710v1"],"cited_by":[{"path":"23-splatting.md","name":"Splatting","k":9},{"path":"19-direct-volume-ray-casting.md","name":"Direct volume ray casting","k":60},{"path":"902-adaptive-octree-construction-with-2-1-balance-enforcement.md","name":"Adaptive Octree Construction with 2:1 Balance Enforcement","k":30},{"path":"1168-solid-voxelization-via-octree.md","name":"Solid Voxelization via Octree","k":2},{"path":"774-marching-cubes.md","name":"Marching Cubes","k":80},{"path":"824-fourier-projection-slice-volume-rendering.md","name":"Fourier Projection-Slice Volume Rendering","k":15},{"path":"1019-early-ray-termination.md","name":"Early ray termination","k":18},{"path":"3020-discrete-ray-tracing.md","name":"Discrete Ray Tracing","k":5},{"path":"1168-hierarchical-splatting.md","name":"Hierarchical Splatting","k":2},{"path":"5648-gradient-based-surface-shading.md","name":"Gradient-Based Surface Shading","k":8},{"path":"3314-indirect-volume-rendering.md","name":"Indirect Volume Rendering","k":2},{"path":"1816-per-voxel-projection-object-order.md","name":"Per-voxel Projection (Object-order)","k":4},{"path":"3161-image-order-ray-casting.md","name":"Image-order Ray-Casting","k":7},{"path":"3594-van-hook-levoy-ray-casting.md","name":"Van Hook-Levoy Ray-Casting","k":3},{"path":"3002-ray-tracing-binary-objects.md","name":"Ray Tracing (Binary Objects)","k":3},{"path":"5750-alpha-blending.md","name":"Alpha Blending","k":4},{"path":"902-maximum-intensity-projection.md","name":"Maximum Intensity Projection","k":30},{"path":"1015-binary-volume-rendering-opacity-thresholding.md","name":"Binary Volume Rendering (Opacity Thresholding)","k":4},{"path":"1184-direct-volume-rendering.md","name":"Direct Volume Rendering","k":15},{"path":"4304-shear-warp-algorithm.md","name":"Shear-Warp Algorithm","k":17},{"path":"5616-hardware-accelerated-volume-rendering.md","name":"Hardware-Accelerated Volume Rendering","k":1},{"path":"26-cell-projection.md","name":"Cell projection","k":3},{"path":"40-illustrative-and-non-photorealistic-volume-rendering.md","name":"Illustrative and non-photorealistic volume rendering","k":3},{"path":"5754-homogeneity-acceleration.md","name":"Homogeneity Acceleration","k":2},{"path":"5752-mueller-s-splatting-approach.md","name":"Mueller's Splatting Approach","k":4},{"path":"6304-volumetric-attribute-and-density-formation.md","name":"Volumetric Attribute and Density Formation","k":1},{"path":"5725-screen-parallel-rendering.md","name":"Screen Parallel Rendering","k":3},{"path":"5721-extraction-of-surface-points-sobierajski.md","name":"Extraction of Surface Points (Sobierajski)","k":1},{"path":"5716-mixed-modality-visualization.md","name":"Mixed Modality Visualization","k":1},{"path":"5713-diffusion-tensor-imaging-dti-visualization.md","name":"Diffusion Tensor Imaging (DTI) Visualization","k":1},{"path":"5715-multi-subject-medical-visualization.md","name":"Multi-Subject Medical Visualization","k":1},{"path":"5753-presence-acceleration.md","name":"Presence Acceleration","k":2},{"path":"5720-distance-transformation-proximity-clouds.md","name":"Distance Transformation (Proximity Clouds)","k":2},{"path":"6054-local-maximum-intensity-projection.md","name":"Local Maximum Intensity Projection","k":5},{"path":"6053-isosurface-display-via-opacity-mapping.md","name":"Isosurface Display via Opacity Mapping","k":1},{"path":"6192-gpu-raycasting.md","name":"GPU Raycasting","k":3},{"path":"5728-object-parallel-rendering.md","name":"Object Parallel Rendering","k":1},{"path":"3161-volume-ray-casting.md","name":"Volume Ray Casting","k":33},{"path":"5746-custom-hardware-rendering.md","name":"Custom Hardware Rendering","k":2},{"path":"4675-early-ray-termination.md","name":"Early Ray Termination","k":24}]}